---
const points = [
  {
    title: 'Thousands of tiny plots',
    body: 'Smallholder farms under 4 ha are points, not polygons, under the regulation. In Ghana, Côte d’Ivoire, Ecuador, Peru, Cameroon and Nigeria, plot data arrives from co-ops in whatever shape the co-op keeps it, and it still has to reconcile.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Aggregation and blending',
    body: 'Beans from many farms become one lot, one container, one shipment. Grovetrace models the join explicitly, so a filed DDS can name every plot behind a blended batch.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Co-ops sit in the middle of the chain',
    body: 'Your supplier is usually a cooperative, not the farmer. Grovetrace records the consolidation step itself (farmer batch, co-op, exporter) so the plots behind a co-op delivery stay traceable instead of disappearing at the point of aggregation.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The systems cocoa actually runs',
    body: 'Field-data tools, ERP exports and co-op spreadsheets, ingested where they are. No rip-and-replace, because origin will not adopt your software.',
  },
];
---
<section class="cocoa">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why cocoa</span>
    <h2>Built for cocoa first</h2>
    <p class="intro prose">
      Plenty of tools claim cocoa. The difference shows up in the parts that are
      tedious to get right, the ones that decide whether a DDS can actually be
      filed for a real, blended shipment.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      {points.map((p) => (
        <div class="card reveal lift">
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p>{p.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cocoa { padding: var(--section-y) 0; }
  .intro { color: var(--muted-foreground); margin: 14px 0 32px; }
  /* 340px rather than 280px so the four cards land 2x2 instead of 3 + an
     orphan on its own row. Chosen as the widest track that still gives two
     columns at 768px (a 360px track dropped the tablet to one), and it falls
     to a single column below ~600px. */
  .grid { display: grid; gap: 16px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(340px, 100%), 1fr)); }
  .card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border);
          border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 20px 22px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
  h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .card p { color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: 0.97rem; }
</style>
